GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":33190}]},"standards":{"engine":"standards","checks":[{"id":"schema-gov","label":"schema.org GovernmentOrganization markup","pass":false,"detail":""},{"id":"canonical","label":"Canonical URL declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"hreflang","label":"hreflang alternates declared","pass":false,"detail":""},{"id":"title","label":"Page has a <title>","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"description","label":"Meta description present","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"charset","label":"Character encoding declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"lang","label":"Document language (lang) set","pass":true,"detail":"en"},{"id":"viewport","label":"Responsive viewport (zoom not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Center for Innovation in Risk, Catastrophes, and Decisions (CIRCAD)","description":"The Center for Innovation in Risk, Catastrophes, and Decisions (CIRCAD) is an interdisciplinary, solution-oriented research center dedicated to addressing the escalating financial and societal consequences of natural hazards, extreme events, and systemic disruptions. As disaster-related losses accelerate, insurers face increasing challenges in maintaining coverage availability and affordability, while households, communities, and capital markets confront growing exposure and uncertainty.CIRCAD offers a novel response: a structured partnership that brings together academic researchers, industry leaders, policymakers, and community stakeholders to co-produce tools, models, and strategies essential for navigating a complex and evolving risk landscape. Through this convening role, CIRCAD aligns cutting-edge research with the real-world priorities of insurers and risk managers, advancing data-driven decision frameworks, next-generation insurance products, and innovative risk-transfer mechanisms.In parallel, CIRCAD serves as a hub for professional training and workforce development, engaging students, postdoctoral researchers, and practitioners in interdisciplinary, applied research. These efforts strengthen the sector’s technical capacity while positioning insurance, reinsurance, and financial services as central actors in advancing national resilience.","url":"/centers/center-for-innovation-in-risk-catastrophes-and-decisions-circad/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-innovation-in-risk-catastrophes-and-decisions-circad/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-innovation-in-risk-catastrophes-and-decisions-circad/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-innovation-in-risk-catastrophes-and-decisions-circad/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-innovation-in-risk-catastrophes-and-decisions-circad/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is installed or bookmarked."},{"id":"pwa-apple-touch-icon","label":"Apple touch icon (iOS/bookmark icon)","stat